  "id": "crisis-intervention",
  "term": "Crisis Intervention",
  "definition": "Crisis intervention is a short-term therapeutic response to an acute psychiatric emergency that aims to reduce immediate distress rather than provide a full cure. It can be used in places such as hospitals, the home, or wherever the crisis occurs, with attention to the person’s relationships, inner psychological state, and surroundings.",
